  "answer": {
    "question_id": "H5",
    "status": "answered",
    "text": "The graph does not record per-column CTE filters, and the explain output cuts off before the CTE bodies, so I could not confirm which CTEs are LEFT-JOINed. These result columns have a conditional value edge from a column that looks like a filter. Probable match: contact_role and primary_email, both from crm.contact.is_primary (edges 4f95785a3ee544ce41206617 and d4f3b9ad4f6ed566f676f14a), and status_name, from gold.dim_status.datasource_num_id (73f858abb2b6c6e1563df64f). Uncertain, could be CASE logic or join keys: carrier_name (shipment_id, carrier_code), Ship To Site and site_segment (crm.customer_site.country_code). Columns with only identity or derived edges show no such effect. The query-wide pre-aggregation filters (for example line_status and is_deleted) apply to the whole result and do not make single columns NULL.",
